; ============================================================
; TITLE:    Circles of Circles
; CATEGORY: Fractals
; LEVEL:    Beginner
; TAGS:     recursion, circles, ARC, fractal
; SUMMARY:  Draws a circle with four half sized circles around it, and so on down.
; ============================================================
;
; WHAT IT DOES
;   A big circle sits in the middle. Touching it on the left, right,
;   top and bottom are circles half as big. Each of those has its
;   own smaller circles, making a pattern like a flower or a snowflake.
;
; HOW TO USE
;   Press Run. Change the depth or radius on the last line.
;
; CONCEPTS YOU WILL LEARN
;   * ARC to draw a circle around the turtle
;   * recursion with a list of directions
;   * using FOREACH to visit each direction
;   * stepping out and coming back so the turtle ends where it began
;
; THINGS TO TRY
;   * Use only the left and right directions: [90 270].
;   * Use six directions, every 60 degrees.
;   * Change the shrink ratio from 0.5 to 0.45 so the circles separate.
; ============================================================

; BUBBLE draws a circle of radius :r centered on the turtle, then a
; smaller circle in every direction in :ways.
to bubble :r :depth :ways
  if :depth = 0 [stop]
  setpencolor item :depth [12 3 5 1 13]
  setpensize :depth
  ; ARC 360 draws a full circle around the turtle without moving it.
  arc 360 :r
  foreach :ways [
    ; Point one way and step out to the center of the small circle:
    ; the big radius plus the small radius, so the circles just touch.
    setheading ?
    penup forward :r * 1.5 pendown
    ; A child never sends a circle straight back toward its parent,
    ; so the opposite direction is left out of its list.
    bubble :r / 2 :depth - 1 remove remainder ? + 180 360 :ways
    ; Come home again, facing the same way, for the next direction.
    setheading ?
    penup back :r * 1.5 pendown
  ]
end

clearscreen hideturtle
setbackground [255 250 235]
bubble 100 5 [0 90 180 270]
